This is a textbook case of **coverage-padding tests** — every production method is called (giving 95%+ line coverage), but almost nothing is actually verified. Here's the severity-ranked audit:

---

## 🔴 CRITICAL — Assert-Free Tests (fire-and-forget)

These tests execute code but assert **nothing**, so any behavioral regression passes silently.

### 1. `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)
Calls `AddProduct` but never verifies the product was stored.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(stored);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", stored.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, stored.Price);
```

### 2. `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)
Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price actually changed. Production could silently save the old price.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

### 3. `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)
Calls `RemoveProduct` but never verifies the product is gone. A no-op `Delete` would pass.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

### 4. `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)
Calls `GetProductCount` on an **empty** catalog and discards the result. Doubly broken: no data setup + no assertion.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-002", "Gadget", 19.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(2, _catalog.GetProductCount());
```

### 5. `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)
Applies 10% discount but never checks resulting prices. The discount formula (`Price * (1 - fraction)`) could be wrong and this test would still pass.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);
```

### 6. `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 84)
Imports CSV but never verifies any product was actually created.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var p = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(p);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", p.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, p.Price);
